## How it works

Run it before reading any metric. A mismatch between the arm sizes and the
planned split means assignment, logging or a filter lost paths from one arm,
and every comparison of the experiment is suspect until the cause is found.
`by=` repeats the check per day of assignment or per segment fixed at
assignment; a segment computed after exposure is not a valid `by`.

The result's `reading` puts the check in one sentence: `"expected 50/50,
observed 5040/4960 (control/treatment), p 0.42: no mismatch"`, or
`"mismatch: ... — the test is invalid until the assignment is fixed"` when the
split is off or paths carry two arms. With `by=` it also names the groups that
mismatch: a logging bug on one platform can hide inside a plausible overall
split.

